    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-055: CSS shorthand `background:` (color forms)**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (~50 lines + 5 tests) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## What this ADR corrects\n\n**ADR-054's finding was imprecise.** The ADR-054 fixture used `background: #d35400; border: 2px solid #333` and both silently produced no visible fill, so ADR-054 recorded \"shorthand background: and border: don't parse yet.\"\n\n**That collapsed two independent issues.** A 4-row isolation fixture proves:\n\n| Row | Background | Border | Rendered |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | longhand | longhand | **GREEN fill + border** |\n| 2 | **shorthand** | longhand | **white fill + border** |\n| 3 | longhand | **shorthand** | **orange fill + border** |\n| 4 | both shorthand | | white fill + border |\n\n**`border:` already works** — ADR-040 shipped `try_expand_border` at `stylesheet.cpp:482`, tested at 889-1002. ADR-054's border was rendered (thin 2px line) but invisible against white at small size.\n\n**`background:` fails** — no `try_expand_background` in the dispatcher.\n\n## Wikipedia `background:` usage (site.styles, 141KB)\n\n11 unique values:\n\n| Form | Examples | Count |\n|---|---|---|\n| Color-only | `#fff`, `#ffffff`, `#fff !important`, `var(--x, #fff)` | 5 |\n| `none` | `none`, `none !important` | 2 |\n| `url(...)` + extras | `#fff url(...) repeat`, `url(...) no-repeat right` | 3 |\n| `linear-gradient` | | 1 |\n\n**Color-only + none = 7/11 forms** — most common, cheapest.\n\n## Scope (smaller than expected)\n\nMost infrastructure exists:\n\n- `parse_color` (ADR-013) — shipped\n- `expand_shorthand` dispatcher (ADR-028/040) — shipped\n- `!important` extraction (split_declarations) — shipped\n- `var()` resolution (ADR-026) — shipped, happens before parser sees value\n\nWhat's new: `try_expand_background` (~30 lines) + dispatcher hook (~5 lines) + 5 tests + fixture.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**Color-only v1, not URL v1**: URL forms need `background-image` + `background-repeat` + `background-position` + `background-size` coordination — each with its own keyword grammar (`no-repeat`, `right`, `100% 50%`, `1.23em`, `/size`). That's an ADR of its own (comparable to ADR-040's border work).\n\n**Drop URL/gradient/multi-layer entirely, not half-parse**: extracting only the color from `background: #fff url(x) repeat` produces a **worse** state than dropping — box gets color but no image, whereas today it gets neither. Consistency with `border`/`grid-template`/`flex` malformed handling: drop the whole declaration.\n\n**`background: none` → `background-color: transparent`**: matches CSS spec, equivalent to today's no-op.\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Synthetic fixture: visible delta.** Rows 2 and 4 currently white, will become blue/purple after implementation.\n\n**Wikipedia: 7/11 color forms render** for the first time — article chrome backgrounds, white content backgrounds.\n\n**4/11 URL and gradient forms remain dropped** — no regression, same state as today.\n\n## Deferred\n\n- URL forms (3 forms in Wikipedia CSS)\n- linear-gradient (1 form, no gradient support in paint)\n- Multi-layer (`url(a), url(b)`) — rare\n- `#fff url(...) repeat` compound (part of URL forms work)\n- `background-size` / `-position` / `-repeat` shorthand sub-parsing\n\n## Test plan\n\n~5 new tests:\n1. `background: #fff` → `background-color: #fff`\n2. `background: #2980b9` → `background-color: #2980b9`\n3. `background: none` → `background-color: transparent`\n4. `background: #fff !important` → preserves `!important`\n5. `background: url(x) #fff` → declaration dropped\n6. `background: linear-gradient(...)` → dropped\n\nRefs #245\n",
